<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  `F-158` — the gold disc the slash sits in.

  Straight from page 23 of the owner's PDF. The assistant bubble there is a
  green pill whose glyph is not painted onto the pill: it sits in its own
  **dark circle** at the leading end. That one detail is what keeps the mark
  readable while the pill is expanding, because the glyph never has to share a
  background with the text beside it.

  It is also what makes the collapsed state work. When the label is hidden the
  disc IS the bubble's visible content, so a 48 dp circle does not read as a
  32 dp glyph floating in too much space - it reads as a mark on a ground, at
  both widths, with nothing switching between them.

  SWIP inverts the reference's polarity: gold disc on an ink pill rather than
  dark on bright, because gold on ink is SWIP's pairing and `swip_bubble_bg`
  is already the ink.
-->
<shape xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:shape="oval">
    <solid android:color="@color/swip_icon_background" />
</shape>
